cmd-137b7cf1fb5048eb","cmd-0a7db88133414b1d","cmd-653ad73915e64e70","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"The requested daily maintenance schedule and append-only log retention are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete: healthy pre-restart state and boot identity were captured, the restart was acknowledged, the boot identity changed, and cron, its configuration, retained log data, and command execution recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["The evidence window did not include a naturally occurring 02:15 cron invocation; schedule execution is established by the exact installed cron definition, active/enabled cron service, and successful bounded executions using the same command and redirection.","Lifecycle snapshots are generic and do not inventory /etc/cron.d/inventory-maintenance or the requested log directly; their final state is instead established by executor commands."]}
